---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import IssHeroVideo from '../components/IssHeroVideo.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="International Space Station"
  description="ISS overview: international partnership, on-orbit operations, research, and logistics in low Earth orbit."
>
  <section class="page-home-hero">
    <IssHeroVideo />
    <div class="page-home-hero-inner">
      <p class="page-home-hero-eyebrow">Low Earth Orbit</p>
      <h1 class="page-home-hero-heading">International Space Station</h1>
      <p class="page-home-hero-lead">
        A permanently crewed orbital laboratory where research, operations, and international cooperation run every day.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pb-24 md:px-8">
    <PageHero
      eyebrow="Mission context"
      title="How the ISS works day to day"
      subtitle="A permanently crewed orbital laboratory where multiple agencies run science, technology demonstrations, and long-duration human-spaceflight operations."
    />

    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-void-850/40 p-6 md:p-8">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-white">What the ISS is</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate-300">
          The ISS is a modular station in low Earth orbit assembled over many years by an international partnership led
          by NASA and Roscosmos with major contributions from ESA, JAXA, and CSA. It serves as both a science platform
          and an operational testbed for deep-space mission planning.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-void-850/40 p-6 md:p-8">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-white">What crews do onboard</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> Microgravity research (biology, medicine, fluid physics, materials)</li>
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> Technology demos for exploration systems and life support</li>
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> Maintenance, robotics operations, and occasional EVA/spacewalks</li>
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> Earth observation and educational outreach</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-nebula/20 bg-nebula/5 p-6 md:p-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-white">Operations rhythm</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-300">
        Crew rotations, cargo deliveries, and timeline planning are coordinated from multiple control centers. Mission
        planning balances science time, hardware reliability, visiting vehicle traffic, and crew health constraints.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-void-850/40 p-6 md:p-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-white">Quick facts</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 text-sm text-slate-300 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-void-900/40 p-4">
          <p class="text-slate-500">Orbit type</p>
          <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-slate-200">Low Earth orbit</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-void-900/40 p-4">
          <p class="text-slate-500">Typical altitude</p>
          <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-slate-200">~400 km</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-void-900/40 p-4">
          <p class="text-slate-500">Orbital period</p>
          <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-slate-200">~90 minutes</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-void-900/40 p-4">
          <p class="text-slate-500">Partners</p>
          <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-slate-200">NASA, Roscosmos, ESA, JAXA, CSA</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
